; claude: game AI, from scratch, for teaching: one idea per module, each
; .mli with its diagram, worked example and references, like physics/
; and audio/. Independent of the Playground. Pure OCaml, so every
; backend, the web one included, can use it.
;
; A library per subdirectory (ai/README.md says which and why); this
; one, 'ai', has no module of its own: it is all of them, for the games
; and examples that say (libraries ai).
(library
 (name ai)
 (package elm_playground)
 (wrapped false) ; claude: wrapped, dune would make it a module Ai, hiding the Playground's Ai
 (modules)
 (libraries ai_movement ai_decision ai_search ai_bots ai_learning)
)
